  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">An Integrated multi-sectoral emergency support to returnees in Asgede and Selekleka woredas, Tigray Region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtThis project aims to provide a comprehensive and life-saving response to conflict-affected communities in Asgede and Selkleka woredas. The implementing organization, DPO, along with its sub-implementing partners, is undertaking a multi-sectoral approach to address the urgent needs identified through a recent assessment. The sectors that will be targeted include WASH (Water, Sanitation, and Hygiene), ESNFI (Emergency Shelter and Non-Food Items), Education, CCCM and MPC activities.ltbrgtThe DPO&#x2019;s assessment has revealed critical findings across the identified sectors of intervention. In terms of shelter, there is a severe shortage of shelters, with IDPs residing in overcrowded conditions within classrooms, lacking privacy and basic NFI kits. WASH facilities are compromised, with non-functional shallow well hand pumps, partially functional toilets, and a need for water treatment supplies. The education sector has been significantly impacted, leading to a halt in children&#x2019;s attendance due to damaged infrastructure, displacement, and economic pressures. The assessment underscores the urgent need for intervention and support in these key areas. ltbrgtIn response to these identified needs, DPO is planning to implement a range of multi-sectoral activities. These include the provision of alternative shelter through construction of duplex shelters and rental assistance, provision of NFIs, initiatives to promote education through back-to-school campaigns and basic repairs to school infrastructure and CCCM at the shelter centers. Additionally, WASH activities will focus on desludging latrine facilities and the maintenance of water supply systems in target schools. Lastly, MPC support will be provided to help affected communities strengthen their livelihoods. By addressing these urgent needs across the sectors, the aim is to provide integrated and tailored support to the conflict-affected communities in the two woredas.ltbrgtlt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
